        <section id="workspace" aria-labelledby="workspace-title">
          <h1 class="page-title" id="workspace-title">Saving your work</h1>
          <p class="intro">Read this before you leave work in a browser tab. A run in the browser saves the whole
            machine locally: memory, processes and the files it wrote, plus the terminal. Nothing is sent to a
            server.</p>
          <p>Pick where saves go:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Browser, automatic</strong> is the default: every minute while the page is visible (or every 5
              or 15 minutes, or only on Save now).</li>
            <li><strong>Backup file</strong> downloads a <code>.snowglobe</code> file you can restore later. Backups
              can hold passwords, tokens and database contents and are not encrypted: keep them private, and restore
              only files you trust.</li>
            <li><strong>Folder, automatic</strong> saves into a folder you pick, on browsers with
              <code>showDirectoryPicker()</code> (desktop Chrome and Edge).</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="note">
            <p>A refresh resumes the last completed save, not necessarily your latest changes. Use
              <strong>Save now</strong> before leaving important work.</p>
          </div>
          <p>Saves are tied to the exact site build. After an incompatible rebuild, older ones are kept for export
            rather than restored.</p>
          <p>The agent page keeps machines differently: see
            <a href="../agents/#suspend">machines awake and asleep</a>.</p>
        </section>
